  "decision_date": "10/11/2005",
  "description": "Dividing single house into one-5 bedroom house and one-three bedroom house with Parking and erection of three storey staircase to create an access to 44A Ennismore Avenue.",
  "site_name": "44",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "21/11/2005",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "W4 1SF",
  "street_name": "Ennismore Avenue",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major all other major developments",
  "lapsed_date": "09/11/2010",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The proposed division of the existing single house into one 5-bedroom house and one three-bedroom house with parking and erection of three-storey staircase to create an access to 44A Ennismore Avenue, as shown on drawing numbers 834.01, 834.02 A, and 834.03 A, received 27 September 2005, is recommended for approval as the proposal would not unduly harm the appearance of the existing building or street scene or unduly reduce the amenity of surrounding neighbours. Therefore the proposed development would be contrary to the relevant London Borough of Hounslow Unitary Development Plan 2003 policies; ENV-B.1.1 New Development, H.3.4 Conversions of Houses to Flats andH.6.4 Extensions and Alterations, and Supplementary Planning Guidance 1997.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building.",
    "Condition : 4 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 5 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development Order) 1995 (or any order revoking or re-enacting that order) no enlargement of the premises or any additional structures/buildings within the curtilage of the site shall be carried out.",
    "Condition : 6 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 (or any order revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification), no garages shall be erected [other than those expressly authorised by this permission].",
    "Condition : 7 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 ((or any order revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification), no fences, gates or walls shall be erected within the curtilage of any dwellinghouse forward of any wall of that dwellinghouse which fronts onto a road",
    "Condition : 8 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 (or any order revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification), no windows/dormer windows [other than those expressly authorised by this permission] shall be constructed.",
    "Condition : 9 - The garage or car parking accommodation shown on drawing No. 834.02 shall be provided before the dwelling to which it relates is occupied and thereafter it shall not be used for any purpose other than the parking of vehicles.",
    "Condition : 10 - Before the development is commenced a scheme for protecting the proposed residential accommodation from excessive external noise shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and any works which form part of such a scheme shall be completed before any part of the development is first occupied or used."
  ],
